  "source": {
    "title": "Lurgan Mail, 24 January 1920, p. 5 (\"Municipal Election: The Results: Labour in the Majority\", with the count-by-count account)",
    "publisher": "Lurgan Mail (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "first preferences add to the printed valid poll; quota = valid / (seats + 1) + 1 as printed; each surplus equals the elected candidate's total less the quota and equals the printed transfers; each count is the previous count plus the transfers. Two OCR misreadings corrected by that arithmetic (McCluskey's surplus 64, not 61; O'Neill's share 34, not 84)"
  },
  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920, counted by F. W. Pollock, town clerk. North Area, six seats: 1,534 on the register, 859 valid votes, 55 spoilt. Seven counts; elected in the order McCluskey, Cummins, Levin, Brady, O'Neill, Mahaffy. Eleven of Thompson's 43 papers showed no further preference. Forenames and labels from the list of results."
